ios: keyboard follows the game's text inputs

MobileKeyboard (overridden to call lcHost.keyboard on iOS) is now driven by one place,
syncMobileKeyboard(), run once per client cycle on mobile. It derives the typing context in
handleInputKey()'s order ('login-user' | 'login-pass' | 'report' | 'social' | 'dialog' | 'chat' | null,
the host keyboard kinds of ARCHITECTURE.md §7) and acts on changes only (edge-triggered, so a keyboard
the player dismissed stays down until the next change):
- opening the amount dialog (P_COUNTDIALOG), report abuse (button or menu option) or social input
  (add/delete friend or ignore, private message) shows the keyboard; upstream never showed it for
  social input, and its two direct show() calls ran outside a user gesture, which WKWebView ignores
  (they are replaced by the sync);
- switching login field (Enter or tap) while the keyboard is up re-shows it so the host can update
  its prompt / secure entry; any other change while it is up (input closed, logged in, logged out,
  chat modal opened) hides it.
Taps: a tap on an input area always (re)shows the keyboard (upstream hid it when you tapped from the
username to the password field) and selects the tapped login field first, so the host sees the right
context synchronously.

